                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Square Heroes is a multiplayer focused arena shooter from Australian Developer Gnomic Studios. In Square Heroes you create your owngenetically engineered killing machine that's only goal in life is to kill anything that moves, fight off aliens or even collect gnomes because gnomes are cool.\n\n+Nice cartoony graphics\n+Characters, both player and computer are well designed and somewhat remind me of BattleBlock's design\n+Quite a few different maps, each in a different environment\n+Quite a few different game modes ranging from Team Deathmatch to Gnome Hunt\n+Lots of weapons to unlock as you level up\n+Lots of character headwear to unlock as you complete achievements, each one has a different buff and debuff that goes with it\n+Great AI with different difficulty settings\n+Takes a fair few kills to unlock your weapons once in a match which means it's difficult for someone to get miles ahead of everyone else\n+Super simple controls\n+Bucket loads of fun when playing with friends\n+No idea how they achieved this but even when players have a super high ping the gameplay is still super smooth and there's very little lag\n+Nice music and sound effects\n+Has great local co-op and you can still play online even with four local players\n+Has a Achievement Hunter reference, as an AH fan this makes me very happy\n+Awesome devs who are super friendly, very active in the forums and fix issues with the game very quickly\n\n+/-The devs have focused on getting the multiplayer right and have neglected the singleplayer portion of the game, if you're looking for MP only then that's great but if you want some good SP too you might be disappointed\n\n-You can't create private matches, kind of annoying if you're trying to play with five friends and a random player joins\n-Apart from changing your character's colour and their headwear there's not much in the way of character customisation\n\nVerdict:\n8.5\n\nA super fun multiplayer experience with nice cartoony graphics, well designed characters, lots of unlockables and great devs to back it all up. If you're looking for a fun multiplayer experience with friends I strongly suggest you picking this awesome game up!\n\n***This review was written using a key provided by the Developer for review purposes***\n\nEl K.",
